---
import RenewalGuide from "../../components/astro/RenewalGuide.astro";
const props = {
  title: "How to copy line items onto a renewal deal in HubSpot",
  description: "Compare native product-based line-item creation with copying negotiated deal lines. Map renewal prices and terms, reconcile totals and test retries before launch.",
  h1: "How to carry your line items onto a renewal, exactly",
  intro: "Choose the accepted source lines and the terms that belong on the renewal. Native creation can add product-based line items; copying a negotiated agreement's prices, discounts and dates is a separate requirement to verify.",
  steps: [
    { n: 1, t: "Choose catalog creation or source-line copying", body: "HubSpot's <a href='https://knowledge.hubspot.com/workflows/create-records-with-workflows'>Create record action</a> can add a product-based line item to a new deal. Use that route when it meets the intended target configuration. If the target must preserve negotiated source values, specify those values and test the native, app or API route against them." },
    { n: 2, t: "Map independent target line items", body: "For an API copy, identify the accepted source deal and target, read the source lines, then create separate target line-item records with the intended quantity, price, discount, recurrence and term. Verify writable properties, permissions and associations. Retain the returned target IDs so retries can identify work already completed." },
    { n: 3, t: "Apply the approved renewal scope", body: "Exclude one-time onboarding or implementation fees only when the accepted renewal scope excludes them. A zero-priced line may still describe an included service. Flag retired products for review rather than silently dropping an obligation. Verify connector support for your actual source object and fields." },
    { n: 4, t: "Reconcile and test recovery", body: "Read the target lines back and compare the intended quantities, prices, terms and total. Test a partial failure and repeated request. Resume missing work against the existing target instead of replaying the whole copy blindly." },
  ],
  example: "For a renewal that includes recurring software at $40k and support at $6k but excludes an $8k one-time onboarding fee, the intended annual total is $46k. Reconcile that approved scope before any invoice is generated.",
  template: { href: "/templates/line-item-carryover-reconciliation.csv", label: "Download the line-item carryover reconciliation template (CSV)" },
  burden: "Copying the product name is only part of the job. Confirm the negotiated values, date boundaries and eligible lines, then record how failures and retries are handled. A native action, app or custom integration should pass the same acceptance checks.",
  bridge: "Bring the source agreement, expected renewal lines and one reconciliation example to the discovery call. These define whether native configuration is sufficient and which mapping or recovery requirements need additional implementation.",
  faq: [
    { q: "Can HubSpot workflows add line items?", a: "Yes. The Create record action documents adding product-based line items to a new deal. This does not establish that all negotiated source values are copied. Verify the exact requirement before selecting another tool." },
    { q: "Does a clone app preserve all renewal terms?", a: "That depends on the app and its configuration. Test prices, discounts, quantities, recurrence, dates and one-time exclusions on the same accepted example. Do not infer complete renewal behavior from a successful deal copy." },
  ],
  ctaHeading: "Find the renewals billing the wrong amount",
  ctaBody: "The renewal audit checks your renewal deals against their contracts and flags the ones with missing or mispriced line items, by deal. $600, credited in full toward any build. It starts with a free 30-minute call.",
  relatedPost: { href: "/posts/hubspot-clone-deal-line-items/", label: "HubSpot line-item mapping, reconciliation and retry tests" },
};
---
<RenewalGuide {...props} />
